  "implementation": [
    "The single-file API was replaced in its consumers: PickRequest carries max_files/max_file_bytes/max_total_bytes; FileChooser::choose_files returns Vec<SelectedFile>; Prepared carries Result<Vec<PendingAttachment>, UploadError>. No parallel v1/v2 picker APIs remain.",
    "One portal request and fixed file worker validate every URI before I/O, reject duplicate decoded paths, then open sequentially and enforce file count/individual/aggregate byte limits. Empty selection is invalid; max_total_bytes zero admits only empty files.",
    "Core reserves an entire monotonic token range with checked arithmetic. Picker capacity accounts for current unclaimed draft slots, global entries and live byte-owner leases; files claimed by a pending send are not counted as another draft.",
    "One preparation job reserves all byte and entry leases atomically before reading. Files are read sequentially with descriptor identity/size/mtime/ctime and EOF validation. Failure or cancellation rejects the complete batch; each sealed Bytes owner retains its own lease.",
    "Actor publication revalidates the full scope and batch before inserting any token. A missing/revoked token before UI polling releases every sibling. Rejected payloads and final buffers are dropped in services outside the lightweight UI mutex.",
    "Explicit retry preserves ordered files, original immutable bytes, text/reply and logical nonce; it changes the attempt request. Mock rejects repeated tokens or changed retry bodies. ACKs require distinct nonzero remote attachment identities and expected ordered metadata.",
    "UI applies metadata as one batch revision, preserves previous text/reply/files, rejects empty/partial/obsolete batches and releases all newly returned tokens. Replayed callbacks cannot remove tokens already owned by drafts or pending sends. Prepared list height is bounded using existing limn scroll controls.",
    "Account change/sign-out still delivers one cancellation terminal for the original picker scope, with no file metadata, so the old UI cancellation hold can end. Encoded path separators cannot conceal dot segments from strict URI validation."
  ],
